      "side": 1,
      "message": "Other change-scoped permissions reach the client today through the actions map on ChangeInfo and RevisionInfo, populated by handlers that implement UiAction\u003cChangeResource\u003e (or \u003cRevisionResource\u003e). For example, abandon is exposed via Abandon#getDescription setting setVisible(perm.testCond(ABANDON)), and the UI reads changeInfo.actions[\"abandon\"]. Almost every ChangePermission enum value maps to a UiAction-based entry today (table in the change\u0027s review thread). Plugins can provide their own UIActions.\n\nDELETE_COMMENT permission doesn\u0027t fit that pattern because the REST handlers (DeleteComment, DeleteChangeMessage) are keyed by comment-id / change-message-id — they\u0027re not UiAction\u003cChangeResource\u003es. That\u0027s why we need a separate endpoint for it.\n\nI\u0027m not proposing to move the other permissions to GET /changes/{id}/permissions: the actions map carries more than just permissions (label, title, enabled/disabled with handler-side logic), it\u0027s been part of the public REST API for years, and migrating would break every plugin that reads it.\n\nThe new endpoint is meant specifically for change-scoped permissions whose REST handler doesn\u0027t naturally fit the UiAction pattern, or are UI specific action only, that don\u0027t have REST endpoint handlers at all, like recently introduced AiReview change-scoped permission. I\u0027ll tighten the commit message to make that intent explicit and also extend REST API documentation.",
